        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "55cde291-0d09-5649-86ab-8b6db3b5e04d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lucy Maud Montgomery, Jan Karon\n- Works: Anne of Green Gables, Anne of Avonlea, Anne of Avonlea (1975 film), The Mitford Years\n- Places: Canada, Mitford, North Carolina\n- Topics: Novel series, authorship, adaptations\n\nFacts:\n- Lucy Maud Montgomery was a Canadian author who lived from November 30, 1874 to April 24, 1942 and published as L.M. Montgomery.\n- In 1908, Lucy Maud Montgomery began a series of novels with Anne of Green Gables.\n- Anne of Avonlea is the sequel to Anne of Green Gables by Lucy Maud Montgomery.\n- Anne of Avonlea (1975 film) is based on Anne of Avonlea by Lucy Maud Montgomery.\n- Jan Karon is an American novelist who writes for both adults and young readers.\n- The Mitford Years is a series of ten novels by American writer Jan Karon.\n- The Mitford Years is set in the fictional town of Mitford, North Carolina.",
